/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 760 Tm (L2 regularization adds the sum of squared weights to the loss,) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 742 Tm (scaled by a coefficient lambda. Its effect is to shrink weights) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 724 Tm (toward zero without setting them exactly to zero, which is why it is) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 706 Tm (also called weight decay. When lambda approaches zero the penalty) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 688 Tm (vanishes and the model reduces to ordinary least squares.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 652 Tm (3.4 L1 regularization and sparsity) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 632 Tm (L1 regularization adds the sum of absolute weights. Unlike L2 it) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 614 Tm (tends to drive a subset of weights exactly to zero, producing a) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 596 Tm (sparse solution that can serve as feature selection. Geometrically) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 578 Tm (the constraint region of L1 is a diamond whose vertices lie on the) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 560 Tm (axes, so the optimum often lands on a vertex where some weights) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 542 Tm (are exactly zero.) Tj
